Package: NCVROC
Type: Package
Title: Nested Cross-Validation for Combinatorial ROC-Based Selection of Item-Set Scores
Version: 0.14.0
Authors@R:
    person(
        given = "Sohei",
        family = "Ide",
        email = "sohei@ni.tama.ac.jp",
        role = c("aut", "cre", "cph")
    )
Description: Develops short item-based screening scales through combinatorial
    item-set selection, receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve
    evaluation, and nested cross-validation. For psychological/clinical
    questionnaire data, identifies which small subset of items best predicts
    a binary outcome using simple sum scores. Assumes higher sum scores
    indicate higher probability of a positive outcome. Methods for ROC
    analysis are described by Fawcett (2006)
    <doi:10.1016/j.patrec.2005.10.010>, and nested cross-validation for model
    selection by Varma and Simon (2006) <doi:10.1186/1471-2105-7-91>.
